==Trivia==
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.6 Update|Version 2.0.6]] increased Berserker Cat's Critical Hit chance from 20% to 40%.
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.9 Update|Version 2.0.9]] changed Berserker Cat from Single Attack to Area Attack.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Marauder Cat was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Dynamites (Removed Combo)|Dynamites]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Marauder Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Marauder Cat
Its cursed sword reduces the offensive power
but might deliver critical hits.
Known as the "Metal Killer".</pre>
<pre>Berserker Cat
The cursed sword has taken over and
turned the Cat into the Cursed Knight.
Known as the "Dark Metal Knight". (Area Atk)</pre>
<pre>Paladin Cat
This Cat's righteous heart finally conquered
the cursed sword, turning it into a holy axe.
Might critical attack. (Area Attack)</pre>
**Despite being known as the "Metal Killer" in its original description, Marauder Cat was not retroactively given the [[Metal Killer]] ability after it was added.
**Berserker Cat's original nickname, "Dark Metal Knight", could potentially have been referencing [https://wikirby.com/wiki/Dark_Meta_Knight Dark Meta Knight], a recurring boss in the ''[[wikipedia:Kirby (series)|Kirby]]'' series.
*Berserker Cat is modeled after the gaming magazine [[wikipedia:Famitsu|''Famitsu'']]'s mascot, Necky the Fox, as described in [[Nyanko Ecology Report Large Edition]]. Though at first they would appear to lack any visual similarities, Necky is depicted in a different costume every time he appears on the magazine's cover art, with many of the costumes including dark clothing, a sword, and/or medieval armor.
**Berserker Cat also looks like [[wikia:berserk:Guts|Guts]] from the manga ''[[wikipedia:Berserk (manga)|Berserk]]'' in [[wikia:berserk:Berserker Armor|Berserker Mode]].
*Paladin Cat's weapon looks like a combination of several weapons used by [[wikipedia:Kingdom Hearts|''Kingdom Hearts'']]' Organization XIII: it has Axel's Chakrams, Vexen's Shield, Lexaeus's Axe, Larxene's Knives, and Xaldin's Lances. Paladin Cat himself also shares some similarities with the Twilight Thorn Nobody.
*Paladin Cat's True Form evolution description claims that he is granted "Resistance to enemy attack's knockback", when in reality, he gains a full immunity to knockback.
**This is likely because Immune to Knockback was originally named Resist Knockback.
*There is a typo in Paladin Cat's [[Talents]] screen: it says "Freeeze" instead of freeze.
*With the relevant Ultra Talent fully upgraded and all [[Critical Hit|Critical]] Rate UP [[Cat Combo]]s active, Paladin Cat can achieve the highest sub-100% Critical chance in the game, at 65%.
*Paladin Cat's Zombie Killer Talent may be a reference to how paladins in pop culture (e.g., [[wikipedia:Paladin (Dungeons & Dragons)|''Dungeons & Dragons''<nowiki>'</nowiki> paladin class]]) tend to have holy powers, smiting unholy beings such as the undead. Even in [[The Battle Cats]], the [[Ototo Corps|Holy Blast]] is effective against [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]].

